<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shedet</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Crocodilopolis, Arsinoe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shedet was the chief town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faiyum">Faiyum</a> in ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, on the site of modern Faiyum city, and the main cult centre of the crocodile god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sobek">Sobek</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> called it Crocodilopolis and later Arsinoe. The Twelfth Dynasty kings, who developed the Faiyum, built extensively there.</p></div>
